{# ============================================================================
   /ventures/ — THE RECORD
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   This page deliberately does a DIFFERENT job from the homepage's "One
   Ecosystem" section. The homepage pitches the three ventures to a visitor
   with photography and scroll choreography. This page is the reference
   record for the audience this site actually serves — partners,
   institutions and press. Same three subjects, opposite register: a
   document, not a story.

   Structural devices are therefore documentary, not editorial: a masthead
   record strip of hard facts, then one specification band per venture with
   a mono label/value ledger. No photography (the homepage owns that), no
   sticky column, no drag-scrub, no cards, no ghost numerals — the homepage
   already uses 01/02/03 ghost numbers in two separate sections, and
   repeating them here is exactly how five pages collapse into one template.

   FRAMING CORRECTION (2026-08-26): this page previously opened with
   "three distinct stages of the same journey". docs/01-AUDIT.md establishes
   that Admizz Workforce Solutions is US vocational rehabilitation —
   supported employment and job coaching for individuals with disabilities,
   working with the state department. It is not the careers arm of a
   study-abroad company, and the sequential "one journey" claim is factually
   strained. Reframed as three businesses under one group. NOTE: the
   homepage's ecosystem section still carries the original framing; it is
   frozen in this branch and is queued for a separate, reviewable change.
   ============================================================================ #}

{# ============================================================ MASTHEAD
   A document header, not a marketing hero: title, then a record strip of
   hard facts read straight from site.json. Every value here is real —
   nothing about scale, reach or outcomes, because none of that is verified
   anywhere in this repo. #}
<section class="bg-navy-deep py-section">
  <div class="shell">
    <span class="eyebrow-on-navy fade-up">The Record</span>
    <h1 class="mt-4 font-display font-light text-display-2 text-navy-on max-w-[15ch] text-balance fade-up" style="animation-delay:80ms">
      Three businesses, <em class="italic text-navy-accent font-book">one group.</em>
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 text-body-lg text-navy-on-muted max-w-measure leading-relaxed fade-up" style="animation-delay:140ms">
      Admizz Institute, Admizz Education and Admizz Workforce Solutions each serve a different audience and answer to a different market. What they share is a conviction that access to opportunity shouldn&rsquo;t depend on where someone starts.
    </p>

    {# Record strip — hard facts only, mono, hairline-separated. The device
       that tells a visitor within one second that this page is a reference
       document rather than another pitch. #}
    <dl class="record-strip mt-12 fade-up" style="animation-delay:200ms">
      <div class="record-strip-item">
        <dt class="data-label-on-navy">Group</dt>
        <dd class="mt-1.5 text-small text-navy-on font-medium">{{ site.legalName }}</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="record-strip-item">
        <dt class="data-label-on-navy">Established</dt>
        <dd class="mt-1.5 text-small text-navy-on font-medium tabular-nums">{{ site.founded }}</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="record-strip-item">
        <dt class="data-label-on-navy">Headquarters</dt>
        <dd class="mt-1.5 text-small text-navy-on font-medium">{{ site.address }}</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="record-strip-item">
        <dt class="data-label-on-navy">Businesses</dt>
        <dd class="mt-1.5 text-small text-navy-on font-medium">Three</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>

{# ============================================================ THE THREE RECORDS
   One specification band per venture. The bands share a structure on
   purpose — a spec sheet with inconsistent fields is a worse spec sheet —
   and the variation between them comes from the DATA being genuinely
   different, not from arbitrary layout changes: Institute carries five
   examinations and no public site, Education carries the group's only
   accreditation, Workforce carries neither. #}
<section class="bg-paper py-section">
  <div class="shell">

    {% for v in ventures %}
    <article class="venture-record" data-venture-record>
      {# Hairline ruled across by GSAP DrawSVG as the band enters (main.js).
         Renders FULLY DRAWN with no JS — the base state is always the
         finished one (see the scroll-reveal note in main.css). #}
      <svg class="venture-rule text-rule-strong" height="1" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <line x1="0" y1="0.5" x2="100%" y2="0.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1" vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke"/>
      </svg>

      {# Document header: folio left, classification right, pushed to the
         band's outer edges. Reads as a record header at a glance and puts
         real tension on the band's top edge — where the left rail this
         replaced just left ~600px of dead space on two bands out of three. #}
      <div class="venture-head">
        <span class="font-mono text-micro uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-faint tabular-nums">Record {{ v.index }} / 03</span>
        <span class="font-mono text-micro uppercase tracking-widest text-navy-soft">{{ v.vertical }}</span>
      </div>

      <h2 class="mt-6 font-display font-light text-h1 text-ink text-balance" data-venture-name>{{ v.name }}</h2>

      <p class="mt-5 text-body-lg text-ink leading-snug max-w-measure font-book">{{ v.verticalLine }}</p>
      <p class="mt-5 text-body text-ink-muted leading-relaxed max-w-measure">{{ v.description }}</p>

      {# ---- The ledger: this page's core device ---- #}
      <dl class="venture-ledger mt-12">

        {% if v.exams.length %}
        <div class="venture-ledger-row">
          <dt class="data-label">Examinations</dt>
          <dd class="venture-ledger-value font-mono text-small text-ink tracking-wide">
            {% for e in v.exams %}{{ e }}{% if not loop.last %} <span class="text-ink-faint" aria-hidden="true">/</span> {% endif %}{% endfor %}
          </dd>
        </div>
        {% endif %}

        <div class="venture-ledger-row">
          <dt class="data-label">Accreditation</dt>
          <dd class="venture-ledger-value">
            {% if v.id == "education" %}
            <span class="text-small text-ink">ICEF Accredited Agency &middot; <span class="tabular-nums">IAS 6499</span></span>
            {% else %}
            {# Deliberately not "None". Absence of a listed accreditation is not
               evidence of absence — this states only what the repo can verify. #}
            <span class="text-small text-ink-faint">No accreditation on record</span>
            {% endif %}
          </dd>
        </div>

        <div class="venture-ledger-row">
          <dt class="data-label">Web</dt>
          <dd class="venture-ledger-value">
            {% if v.href == "#" %}
            {# Bug fix: this was an <a href="#"> dressed as a working link.
               hrefLabel exists in ventures.json to solve exactly this and was
               read by no template until now. Rendered as a status, not a link,
               so it is not focusable as though it were one. #}
            <span class="text-small text-ink-faint">{{ v.hrefLabel }}</span>
            {% else %}
            <a href="{{ v.href }}" class="text-small text-ink link-underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{{ v.hrefLabel }}</a>
            {% endif %}
          </dd>
        </div>

        {# Related reading — derived from the venture↔article relationship
           already in insights.json, never a hardcoded slug. #}
        {% for post in insights %}{% if post.venture == v.name %}
        <div class="venture-ledger-row">
          <dt class="data-label">Related reading</dt>
          <dd class="venture-ledger-value">
            <a href="/insights/{{ post.slug }}/" class="text-small text-ink link-underline">{{ post.title }}</a>
            <span class="ml-2 font-mono text-micro uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-faint whitespace-nowrap">{{ post.body | readingTime }} min read</span>
          </dd>
        </div>
        {% endif %}{% endfor %}

      </dl>

      {% if v.id == "education" %}
      {# ICEF — the only accreditation that exists anywhere in this project.
         AIRC, British Council, NAFSA, PIER and ISO were searched for and NOT
         found (docs/01-AUDIT.md). It is held by Admizz Education alone, and the
         scope note says so outright rather than letting a seal on the group's
         page imply group-wide accreditation. Stating precisely what a
         credential does NOT cover reads as more credible than a badge.

         This block is also what breaks the three bands out of lockstep — the
         asymmetry is driven by the data being genuinely different, not by
         varying the layout for its own sake. Flagged with a gold rule rather
         than boxed: gold is a surface/rule/seal here, never text on light. #}
      <div class="icef-seal mt-12" data-icef-seal>
        <svg class="icef-mark" viewBox="0 0 64 64" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
          <circle class="icef-ring" cx="32" cy="32" r="29" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1"/>
          <circle class="icef-ring-inner" cx="32" cy="32" r="23.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.75" opacity="0.5"/>
          <path class="icef-check" d="M22 32.5l7 7 14-15" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
        </svg>
        <div class="icef-body">
          <p class="font-mono text-micro uppercase tracking-widest text-gold-text">ICEF Accredited Agency</p>
          <p class="mt-2.5 text-body text-ink font-medium tabular-nums">IAS 6499</p>
          <p class="mt-0.5 text-small text-ink-muted tabular-nums">Valid 15 April 2026 &ndash; 15 April 2027</p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-small text-ink-muted leading-relaxed max-w-[46ch]">
            Held by Admizz Education. This accreditation does not extend to Admizz Institute or Admizz Workforce Solutions.
          </p>
          <a href="https://accreditations.icef.com/certificate?id=c8a7212a-a25c-469f-8a7b-2b2f047e8c0c"
             class="mt-4 inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-small font-medium text-ink link-underline"
             target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            Verify with ICEF
            <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 10L10 4M10 4H5M10 4v5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
      {% endif %}

    </article>
    {% endfor %}

  </div>
</section>

{# ============================================================ CLOSE
   Deliberately not /about/'s centered navy close — a left-weighted band on
   the sunk paper ground, so two inner pages don't end on the same note. #}
<section class="bg-paper-sunk border-t border-rule py-section-sm">
  <div class="shell grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-[1fr_auto] md:items-end gap-8">
    <div class="fade-up">
      <span class="eyebrow">Enquiries</span>
      <p class="mt-4 font-display font-light text-h2 text-ink max-w-[24ch] text-balance">
        Partnership, press or admissions &mdash; <em class="italic text-navy font-book">start here.</em>
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-body text-ink-muted max-w-measure-tight leading-relaxed">
        Tell us which of the three you need and we&rsquo;ll route it to the right team.
      </p>
    </div>
    <a href="/contact/" class="btn-primary shrink-0 fade-up" style="animation-delay:80ms">Get in touch</a>
  </div>
</section>
